meta {
  name: Media upload intent
  type: http
  seq: 28
}

post {
  url: {{api}}/media/upload-intent
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "kind": "IMAGE",
    "contentType": "image/jpeg",
    "sizeBytes": 20,
    "checksum": "PHRGrKTxmilgJsKwA2/xG0zwslpJR9m54yBBR8s//J0="
  }
}

script:post-response {
  // The URL is a credential for one upload: kept as a runtime variable, never in a file.
  bru.setVar("mediaId", res.body.mediaId);
  bru.setVar("uploadUrl", res.body.uploadUrl);
  bru.setVar("uploadChecksum", res.body.requiredHeaders["x-amz-checksum-sha256"]);
}

docs {
  Asks for a URL to upload one photo or voice note to, straight to the storage (ADR-0047). The example declares the 20 bytes that Upload sends, `fake photo for bruno`, and their SHA-256; change one and the storage refuses the other. 201 with the URL, the headers the upload must carry, and when the URL stops working (15 minutes).

  An image is JPEG, PNG, HEIC or WebP and at most 10 MB; a voice note at most 5 MB. Another type is 415 MEDIA_TYPE_UNSUPPORTED, too many bytes 413 MEDIA_QUOTA_EXCEEDED, a missing or malformed field 422. 30 an hour per user. In production, until the bucket exists, every intent is 503 MEDIA_STORAGE_UNAVAILABLE.
}
